PR #68 opened — ledger line rides with the work\" && git push -q origin bead/fw-y1y 2>&1 | grep -v \"^│\\|^┃\\|^╭\\|^╰\\|^ *$\\|summary\\|✔️\" ","timeout":120000,"description":"Commit the pr_opened ledger line and push it"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":3,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":3,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":3,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"general-purpose":3}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":155,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Done. Ran **solo** (`run-context.json: solo=true` — no registration or reservation).\n\n## fw-y1y — PR #68\n\n**Bead:** a merged PR does not close its bead, so the fleet redoes finished work (P1).\n\n**Decision (with the evidence the design note asked for):** the bead preferred a `gh:pr` gate. Verified it does the opposite of what's needed — `bd gate check` closes the *gate* and releases the bead **back into `bd ready`** (fw-62j: PR 24 merged → gate closed → fw-fsa.9 became ready, not closed). A gate would re-dispatch on merge. So: candidate (b), recorded as ADR 0016.\n\n**What I built** (`tools/fleet/board.go`): `fleet reconcile-board [-execute]` — for every open/in-progress bead, ask `gh pr list` whether a PR naming it (`bead/<id>` branch, or titled `<id>: …` / `… (<id>)`) has merged, and `bd close` it with the PR as the reason. Runs for real before every `allocate` and `run`. Refusals: closed-not-merged isn't a merge; merged-beside-open is a stack (kept); ids nest; `Revert` never counts; kill switch checked first; a gh failure **refuses to plan** rather than reading as \"nothing merged\". Also fixed `bd list` silently capping at 50.\n\n**Acceptance criterion:** met by `TestConformanceMergedPRLeavesTheReadyQueue` — real `bd` database, both real-world states (open / in_progress), asserts on `bd ready --json` and that reclaim can't resurrect it.\n\n**Gate:** green on all 4 commits (fmt/vet/vet-conformance/short suite via pre-commit; conformance tests ~40s pass).\n\n**Review panel:** 3 lenses, 15 findings in the ledger — 8 accepted, 4 rejected, 3 deferred. Two flagged by two lenses were real and fixed: `bd close` ran before the kill switch check, and a gh failure had become a warning that `allocate`/`run` planned over.\n\n**Two things for you:**\n1. **Stacking accident.** The worktree was cut from `bead/fw-2oh`, so PR #68 is opened against that branch — *not* a real dependency. `git rebase`/`cherry-pick` are outside my allowlist. Either retarget to `main` **before** merging fw-2oh (or GitHub closes it), or cherry-pick `ac243e2 7eb4cf8 9d81d2f` onto main.\n2. I could not run the live dry run (`go run` not allowlisted). First real invocation: `go run ./tools/fleet reconcile-board` — prints what it would close, touches nothing.\n\nBead left open (PR ≠ closed bead), weight `w:2`, `bead.pr_opened` logged. Nothing abandoned.","ttft_ms":3736,"type":"result","duration_ms":1035596,"uuid":"9f72fc81-8b70-45e0-94b0-ecd56736df18","ttft_stream_ms":3036,"time_to_request_ms":172,"queued_turn_count":0}
